# autotune-digital: Auto Tune multimode (issue #205) REFUSING to run in a digital
# mode.
#
# The radio is in USB-D (the data mode FT8/JS8/WSPR use) and the same APP 6
# "Auto Tune" button is pressed through the user's path (button_action_cb ->
# main_screen_action(ACTION_ATUNE) -> autotune_ui_toggle()). Digital modes are
# explicitly out of scope: the action must reject with
# "Auto Tune: mode unsupported", open NO session, request NO spectrum frame and
# leave the dial untouched - the FT8/JS8/WSPR dial and the nominal data
# frequencies are never moved.
#
# This fixture replaces `autotune-notcw` of issue #190: back then AM was
# unsupported too, now AM/SAM and USB/LSB are supported and the refusal that has
# to stay codified is the digital/FM one (issue #205 section 7).
#
# scenario_settle codifies exactly that: the session never started, the dial is
# still the fixture frequency and no spectrum frame was ever requested. Without
# those checks the bank would capture a quiet dial and report green for a
# function that silently retunes in a digital mode.

name autotune-digital
screen autotune-digital

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb-dig
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
